30,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that all-in rates are easier to track, but we might pay for food we don't eat! Still, it's a fixed number.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The travel options are as tedious as I expected. We either waste days on ferries or get trapped by a bus schedule that ends at seven.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The all-in rates are a double-edged sword. While they provide a fixed number, they can be unfair to those who eat less.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The inns are a disaster. One bathroom for everyone and a strict dinner time? No way. I can't do that again.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems our previous choices of accommodation directly influenced how we interacted. The house was too crowded, yet last year we were too fragmented.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Takumi, if the inns are scary, maybe the offshore house is better? I saw the price for those!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, the offshore house requires the ferry. That means two days of our week are gone just moving. That's unacceptable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, efficiency is important, but a house let as a whole allows for a single, clear payment. It prevents the ""out of pocket"" issue.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Rin, the offshore house only has one bathroom. I'm not waiting in line for an hour just to wash up. I need a real room.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"If we want to avoid feeling crowded but also avoid drifting apart, we need a location that allows for natural breaks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,But a house is like a big adventure! We can cook together and it's one big price tag!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm not interested in an ""adventure"" that involves a 16:20 ferry deadline. The city option is the only one that doesn't steal our time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the city option usually means separate rooms. That leads to fragmented payments and confusion over who paid for what.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,I don't care about the payments. I care about having a door and not being forced to eat at exactly six o'clock.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The city provides the ""absorptive"" space I'm looking for. We can be together, but we can also step away without it being a statement.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I still think the house is the most exciting!,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Excitement is a poor substitute for a full day of actual vacation. Let's be rational.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"If we choose the city, we must agree on a strict payment method beforehand. I will not have the costs fall on the most organized person.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,Just make sure it's not a hostel with shared bathrooms. I'm voting for whatever has the most privacy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree with the city. It balances the need for togetherness with the necessity of individual space.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
